1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,050
Two airline pilots spotted something

2
00:00:02,050 --> 00:00:04,104
impossible at sixteen thousand feet.

3
00:00:04,104 --> 00:00:04,557
A man.

4
00:00:04,557 --> 00:00:05,965
Sitting in a lawn chair.

5
00:00:05,965 --> 00:00:07,799
In 1982, Larry Walters

6
00:00:07,799 --> 00:00:09,332
tied forty-two helium balloons

7
00:00:09,332 --> 00:00:10,040
to a chair in his

8
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:11,394
California backyard.

9
00:00:11,394 --> 00:00:12,974
He expected a gentle ride.

10
00:00:12,974 --> 00:00:13,810
Instead, he shot

11
00:00:13,810 --> 00:00:15,594
nearly three miles into the sky.

12
00:00:15,594 --> 00:00:16,500
He'd brought a pellet gun

13
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:17,405
to pop balloons

14
00:00:17,405 --> 00:00:18,762
and come back down.

15
00:00:18,762 --> 00:00:19,760
But after shooting a few,

16
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:20,759
he dropped the gun.

17
00:00:20,759 --> 00:00:21,699
As the chair descended,

18
00:00:21,699 --> 00:00:22,721
he dumped water ballast

19
00:00:22,721 --> 00:00:24,042
to control his landing.

20
00:00:24,042 --> 00:00:25,412
Then his ropes

21
00:00:25,412 --> 00:00:26,888
snagged power lines.

22
00:00:26,888 --> 00:00:28,281
He made it down alive.

23
00:00:28,281 --> 00:00:29,163
The FAA fined

24
00:00:29,163 --> 00:00:30,779
him fifteen hundred dollars.

25
00:00:30,779 --> 00:00:32,304
And the wildest part?

26
00:00:32,354 --> 00:00:33,294
That same lawn chair

27
00:00:33,294 --> 00:00:35,431
is now in the Smithsonian.
